# Repeat Sequence Identification and Annotation

**De novo repeat library construction with RepeatModeler and genome-wide repeat annotation with RepeatMasker.**

## Overview

Repeat families were identified from the genome assembly using RepeatModeler with the LTR structural discovery module enabled. The resulting custom repeat library was then used by RepeatMasker to annotate repetitive sequences in the same assembly.

The commands below document the supplied **CG64** analysis. For another assembly, replace the FASTA filename, database prefix and repeat-library filename consistently, and use a separate working directory.

## Inputs and software

| Item | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| `CG64.Nuclear.Add.fa` | Input genome assembly in FASTA format |
| RepeatModeler | De novo repeat discovery and family classification |
| RepeatMasker | Genome-wide annotation using the custom library |
| RMBlast, TRF and NINJA | Dependencies explicitly referenced in the supplied command |

RepeatModeler and its LTR structural discovery dependencies must be configured before running. Software versions were not included with the supplied commands; retain the versions and configuration used in the actual analysis.

## 1. Construct the repeat database

Run in the directory containing the genome FASTA:

```bash
BuildDatabase -name CG64 CG64.Nuclear.Add.fa
```

`CG64` is the database prefix used in the next step.

## 2. Identify repeat families with RepeatModeler

```bash
RepeatModeler \
    -pa 60 \
    -LTRStruct \
    -ninja_dir /home/GuanJianTao/Software/NINJA-0.95-cluster_only/NINJA \
    -rmblast_dir /home/GuanJianTao/micromamba/envs/repeatmodeler/bin/ \
    -trf_dir /home/GuanJianTao/micromamba/envs/repeatmodeler/bin/ \
    -database CG64 \
    > run.out 2>&1 &
```

This preserves the supplied analysis settings and dependency paths. The original Bash redirection `>& run.out` has been written as the equivalent `> run.out 2>&1`. The trailing `&` launches the process in the background.

| Parameter | Value | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `-database` | `CG64` | Database created with BuildDatabase |
| `-pa` | `60` | Parallelism setting in the supplied RepeatModeler version |
| `-LTRStruct` | Enabled | Include structural discovery of LTR retrotransposons |
| `-ninja_dir` | Supplied NINJA path | Locate the NINJA dependency |
| `-rmblast_dir` | Supplied environment `bin/` | Locate RMBlast |
| `-trf_dir` | Supplied environment `bin/` | Locate TRF |

Check that the dependency paths satisfy the installed version's requirements, including whether a directory is expected. RepeatModeler parallelism options differ between releases; keep `-pa 60` for the original environment and consult the installed help before adapting the command to another version.

Wait for successful completion before starting RepeatMasker. The custom family library used in the supplied workflow is:

```text
CG64-families.fa
```

Review `run.out` for completion and errors, and confirm that this library is present and nonempty.

## 3. Annotate the genome with RepeatMasker

```bash
RepeatMasker \
    -lib CG64-families.fa \
    -pa 30 \
    -html \
    -gff \
    -dir Masker.out \
    CG64.Nuclear.Add.fa
```

| Parameter | Value | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `-lib` | `CG64-families.fa` | Custom repeat library |
| `-pa` | `30` | Parallel sequence-batch jobs |
| `-html` | Enabled | Additional HTML output |
| `-gff` | Enabled | Additional GFF annotations |
| `-dir` | `Masker.out` | Output directory |

`-pa 30` does not necessarily limit execution to 30 CPU threads: each search job can use multiple threads, depending on the search engine and version. The command uses the locally configured search engine because no explicit engine option is supplied.

## 4. Main outputs

| Output | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| `run.out` | RepeatModeler standard output and error log |
| `CG64-families.fa` | Custom repeat-family library used for annotation |
| `Masker.out/CG64.Nuclear.Add.fa.out` | RepeatMasker repeat-hit annotations |
| `Masker.out/CG64.Nuclear.Add.fa.out.gff` | GFF-format annotations |
| `Masker.out/CG64.Nuclear.Add.fa.out.html` | HTML annotation report |
| `Masker.out/CG64.Nuclear.Add.fa.masked` | Masked genome sequence |
| `Masker.out/CG64.Nuclear.Add.fa.tbl` | Repeat-content summary, when generated by the installed version/configuration |

Additional intermediate files may be produced. Retain the custom library with the annotations to preserve the basis of the repeat calls.


